The tsna package does calculate some temporal network statistics 
directly 
(https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/tsna/vignettes/tsna_vignette.html#temporal-paths-and-metrics) 
without using static network slices. However, although it can calculate 
the 'earliest forward paths' analogous to the shortest paths that would 
be used to compute  temporal betweeness and centrality as in 
https://people.ece.ubc.ca/hyoung/publication/TemporalCentrality_PRE.pdf, 
I don't believe those measures are directly implemented yet.

